{"title":"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(less_casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (less casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of five-digit positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, that satisfy the following conditions:\n</p>\n<ul>\n(a) the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/21415a2eb558eb7c199a0382fcd50cbeda9299fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" />\n</ul>\n<ul>\n(b) the first and last digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are equal, and\n</ul>\n<ul>\n(c) the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b835f2c6c592edc4583ce996f86bcc0d07ca8da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</ul>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number takes a form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f70cceca1319c51924e22dac3b133f6883781dc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{5xyz5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"21\" />, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635ac04ca1de07acb88710b181758718a74f2360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5|(x+y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be arbitrary digits. For each pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />, there are exactly two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy the condition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635ac04ca1de07acb88710b181758718a74f2360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5|(x+y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a898a9b062733191f2d7f727bf500195dcf3ecf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\times10\\times2=\\boxed{200}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(casework)\">Solution 2 (casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know the number will take the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f70cceca1319c51924e22dac3b133f6883781dc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{5xyz5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"21\" /> because of the first two conditions. The third condition means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635ac04ca1de07acb88710b181758718a74f2360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5|(x+y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> are nonnegative integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let's split the problem into cases, where each case represents a possible sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>1. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/948bef8fd29dd497dd9532936d11a5bdb999ded4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />, we only have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d545b6c81b084f60070b1cf24b03c3a38ef98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0,y=0,z=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"17\" />, so only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>2. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1442a36f13aac7c9b450250da6246f1db7549e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />, we use stars &amp; bars. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> stars and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296f0bc50ac812f710edefec4457e24fa31935c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> bars, so this case has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1bb331d47ee0a084ddccd6ad61a84c9f3509b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\choose{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"27\" height=\"28\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a801b46231236d2556e96ad13f00a6515178eed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>3. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da55e0b999f3071becf6ce938ddbfda435276fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, we use similar logic. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> stars and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bars, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a836437dd8c4845ac23a5d7ef6bd89c2ec10251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\choose{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"36\" height=\"28\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/371a6636204ac98380aab06f594df7b66ec5deb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Three of our order pairs have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2ec3763b32386a65181dd2047cc3ae31a113d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10: (10,0,0), (0,10,0), (0,0,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, this case has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d0784180b7c3c653900cf17f9947a7c4ce78482a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66-3=63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>4. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d9005411107577b69da4a1851dd58a82cfcf59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, it gets more complicated. Using the same system as used previously would be too complicated. But remember that this case is equivalentto if we wanted to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/9111f8c10dd1a79d621c1886534f9c0aab401ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />. We know this because you can take any ordered pair satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/00196153eb3c0626056d4d5607570d098c5d8073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=15,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" /> subtract each variable from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and get an ordered pair satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/9111f8c10dd1a79d621c1886534f9c0aab401ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />. For example, take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f33c8a81240ff33abe4a81fa4b858eccd82c7eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,6,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />, which satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4b9f4d8d73e6de4bc9647356b59ce87e7ad238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=15.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" /> Its corresponding ordered pair would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5cb8ad4f71ece332fd067aeeeb53d964c54a3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,3,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />, which satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/9111f8c10dd1a79d621c1886534f9c0aab401ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />. Let's proceed to calculating. Applying stars and bars, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/0035e0c3f2e4630592aa3f20b21ebcd7aed5a4d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14\\choose{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"36\" height=\"28\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca42c7d07fb92803e12361ae1217fd7df6cc191a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />, but we have to subtract the subcases including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d0d7bad937dcd443eacc2601357d21b064003d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10,11,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> must all be one-digit integers. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases with an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/1067acb571cf793276184f650bba767d064cfc7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> cases with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. So this case has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b574197bcb93743d2ae94b179b582afdbce28a82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91-18=73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>5. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1fef8c58fc4b762d0ba9e47f49c37026bb68d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" />, we can just calculate the ways to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9a0ac9ab730c21741d7119080dc3af3471880f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />. Applying stars &amp; bars, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/5/cd5178a958d3e231f07e2ffcb26bf0aa345cd6d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\choose{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"27\" height=\"28\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f2304708929fae648d125c5a142d380d89830d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>6. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496ef2094172037a9fe7751a954e1dd01bdf8023.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, we can just calculate the ways to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cdd4312ff8876fec526b18a68031c6005f0b8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" /> Applying stars &amp; bars, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb97c75c398a3c04e5768a7af27bcd8d5b74f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\choose{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"27\" height=\"28\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f3309537cc68c3ba4b8b7372a483d4f895d376e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 6$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7fcfb21a84791d84d6d2e11a33c13b103f1f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+21+63+73+36+6 = \\boxed{200}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"267\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Note: For case 4, the subcases that must be excluded are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b34342f5922fd30a209c2f6a4ac6951ff2de120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12,0,0), (11,1,0), (10,2,0), (10,1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"293\" height=\"20\" /> and each of their respective permutations. Those <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pairs have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de59d8cbd02b5cc22c7cbfffced9963f974e15cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,6,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> permutations respectively, which is why <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pairs must be subtracted from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28less_casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(less_casework)\">Solution 3 (less casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (less casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Again, from the first two conditions we know the number takes the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f70cceca1319c51924e22dac3b133f6883781dc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{5xyz5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"21\" />, and the third condition implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635ac04ca1de07acb88710b181758718a74f2360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5|(x+y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are less than 5. Now, we will proceed with casework on the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/786294ba81c75be655bda0e12c983b0ef8919a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/948bef8fd29dd497dd9532936d11a5bdb999ded4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are nonnegative, there is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1442a36f13aac7c9b450250da6246f1db7549e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />. Using stars and bars, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14d9f23a212d94792a4666374865ef8e50090b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5+3-1}{3-1} = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"144\" height=\"55\" />. However, we assumed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3fe63f5c9a441f6e40e30daa537520ce63fcd72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />, so we subract 3 to get 18.\n</p><p>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da55e0b999f3071becf6ce938ddbfda435276fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />. Our only possible triplets are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e97a72de1a41e6ab97eac5cef3f05b12ef3ec38c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa911dcfdaf1d7c8d161016c2cab54eeca9a905e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and their rearrangements, totalling <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b0375ea5d39656d7f86f115ebfbed8c55fccb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Due to our assumption that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3fe63f5c9a441f6e40e30daa537520ce63fcd72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/786294ba81c75be655bda0e12c983b0ef8919a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> cannot be 15, so our casework is done. Summing, we find a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a645622363f05276f4ec197d31634794d565c6f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+18+6=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" />. However, for each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we can add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> without violating the conditions. So, we can either choose to add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or not, so we have to multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to our cases three times for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047f87d19e465d9ee07dad3fea419e397030121a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 = \\boxed{200}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"149\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kz3ZX4PT-_0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kz3ZX4PT-_0</a>\n~Shreyas S\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I\" title=\"2013 AIME I\">2013 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231247\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 589/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18030/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.915      1 -total\n 59.87%    8.331      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.08%    5.160      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11837:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231247 and revision id 289662. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}